# Shell scripts must keep LF even when checked out on Windows: a CRLF in
# install.sh makes the `#!/usr/bin/env sh` line unrunnable under WSL and any
# Unix host the clone is copied to, with an error that names no cause.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The PowerShell installer carries a UTF-8 BOM on purpose — Windows PowerShell
# 5.1 reads a BOM-less script as ANSI and mis-parses its box-drawing comments.
*.ps1 -text
